X:1
T:A Lot to Ask
M:4/4
L:1/8
Q:1/4=100
K:G
%%section Verse 1
D2 G2 G2 AB | B2 A2 G2 E2 |
w: You set the a-larm | for half past two |
E2 G2 A2 BA | A2 G2 D4 |
w: And drag a blan-ket | to the roof |
D2 G2 A2 B2 | B2 A2 G2 E2 |
w: The weath-er called | for some-thing new |
E2 G2 A2 BA | A2 G2 G4 |
w: The sky is giv-ing | you no proof |
%%section Chorus
B2 c2 d2 d2 | c2 B2 A2 G2 |
w: Stay a-wake for | the fall-ing light |
d2 d2 c4 | B2 c2 B2 A2 |
w: Noth-ing drops | a-cross the night |
B2 c2 d2 de | d2 c2 B4 |
w: You brought the co-coa | in a flask |
c2 B2 A2 GA | B2 A2 G2 G2 |
w: A me-te-or is | a lot to ask |
%%section Verse 2
D2 G2 G2 AB | B2 A2 G4 |
w: At three the neigh-bour's | porch goes dark |
E2 G2 A2 B2 | A2 B2 A2 G2 |
w: At four a plane | pre-tends to fall |
D2 G2 G2 A2 | B2 A2 G2 E2 |
w: You clap for it, | a bor-rowed spark |
E2 G2 A2 B2 | A2 G2 D2 G2 |
w: It is-n't much, | you'll take it all |
%%section Chorus
B2 c2 d2 d2 | c2 B2 A2 G2 |
w: Stay a-wake for | the fall-ing light |
d2 d2 c4 | B2 c2 B2 A2 |
w: Noth-ing drops | a-cross the night |
B2 c2 d2 de | d2 c2 B4 |
w: You brought the co-coa | in a flask |
c2 B2 A2 GA | B2 A2 G2 G2 |
w: A me-te-or is | a lot to ask |
%%section Bridge
E2 G2 A2 Bc | B2 A2 G2 E2 |
w: The dawn comes up the | col-our of tea |
E2 G2 A2 B2 | c2 B2 A2 A2 |
w: Your blan-ket's damp, | the flask is dry |
E2 G2 A2 B2 | c2 d2 c2 B2 |
w: You did-n't see | a sin-gle streak |
c2 B2 A2 GA | B2 A2 G4 |
w: But you were look-ing | at the sky |
